Sval: remove Firefox's padlock, site button, and reader and split buttons

Sval's protection button replaces the padlock and the site button (decision
0131), and Sval locks browser.urlbar.trustPanel.featureGate off, so
gTrustPanelHandler reads nothing. The site button's readers take a missing
element: _refreshIdentityIcons stops before it writes the button's tooltip
and label, and the padlock's dragstart listener is optional.
PopupNotifications' anchor fallback in browser.js already skips a null
element. Sval's header draws its own reader and split buttons under these
ids, so AboutReaderParent.updateReaderButton, tabsplitview.js's
updateUrlbarButton and the toolbox's click and keypress handlers drive
them.

